<PageTitle>How to play — Interlock Expeditions</PageTitle>
<article class="prose"><h1>How to play</h1><p>Use two devices and talk to each other. Each crew gets different clues and controls.</p>
<h2>Start a room</h2><ol><li><a href="/account">Create a host account</a> and save its recovery key. Guests do not need accounts.</li><li><a href="/host">Choose a story</a> and a time limit.</li><li>Open one crew's console on your device. Send the invitation to the other device and choose the other crew there.</li><li>When both crews have joined, start from the host controls. Keep those controls in another tab if you also play.</li></ol>
<h2>Solve a puzzle</h2><p>Your clue often describes the other crew's controls. Explain it to them and ask what your own settings should be. Changes appear on both consoles automatically.</p><p>For the first five puzzles, both crews press <strong>Check station</strong>. Changing a setting clears earlier checks. A failed check, blocked move or puzzle restart costs five seconds.</p><p>In the final puzzle, both crews press <strong>Arm</strong> within fifteen seconds of each other. Count down together.</p>
<details><summary>What the controls do</summary><ul><li><strong>Dials:</strong> machine crew sets three numbers; signal crew chooses the route.</li><li><strong>Relays:</strong> signal crew sets input lamps; machine crew flips the crossed wires' outputs.</li><li><strong>Trolley:</strong> signal crew sees the map and guides the machine crew. Collect the crate before the exit.</li><li><strong>Cradle:</strong> machine crew loads every crate; signal crew adds ballast. Both loads must match and stay under the limit.</li><li><strong>Seal:</strong> each crew turns one ring using the other crew's clue.</li><li><strong>Final terminals:</strong> arm both terminals before either fifteen-second window expires.</li></ul></details>
<h2>Take a break or reconnect</h2><p>The host can pause the clock and controls. Reopen the room on the same device to continue; clearing site data can lose your player access. Late players join at the current puzzle.</p><details><summary>Invitations and private keys</summary><p>Share the room invitation, never your account recovery key. Keep the crew cards on separate devices. Puzzle solutions are available in the public source; avoid opening them if you want to solve the story yourself.</p><p>The site does not provide voice chat. Talk in person or use your usual call.</p></details><a class="button primary" href="/host">Host a room</a></article>
